.TH ZERODDS-NAMING-SVC.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-naming-svc.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-naming-svc(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/naming-svc.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document configuring the standalone CosNaming daemon. The reader is
.I DaemonConfig::from_config
in
.IR crates/corba-cosnaming/src/naming_daemon.rs .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR log_level " and " naming .
.PP
An unknown key inside a known section, or a value of the wrong type,
stops the start with file and line.
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error .
.SS naming
.TP
.B bind
IIOP listen address. Default
.IR "0.0.0.0:2809" .
.TP
.B advertise_host
The host named in every IOR this daemon hands out, when
.B bind
is a wildcard address. Default
.IR 127.0.0.1 ,
environment
.BR ZERODDS_NAMING_ADVERTISE_HOST .
.TP
.B persist_file
Where the naming graph is saved (atomic write: a sibling temporary file,
then a rename), and read back at start. Without it the graph is
in-memory only and a restart starts empty.
.SS naming.ssliop
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean.
.TP
.B bind
SSLIOP listen address. Default
.IR "0.0.0.0:2810" .
.TP
.B cert_file " / " key_file
Server certificate/key (PEM). Required when
.B enabled
is true.
.TP
.B ca_file
CA bundle client certificates are checked against; required when
.B require_client_cert
is true.
.TP
.B require_client_cert
Boolean: the TLS handshake itself refuses a peer without a certificate
that validates against
.BR ca_file " (mutual TLS)."
.SS naming.csiv2
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Unlike
.BR zerodds-corba-bridged (1),
this daemon has no ACL and no mTLS-identity fallback, so when
.B enabled
is true every request must carry valid GSSUP credentials \(em there is
no additive path around it. Requires
.BR gssup.password_file .
.TP
.B target_supports
List of accepted
.I IdentityToken
forms for CSIv2 identity assertion (Spec \(sc24.2.5): any of
.IR anonymous ", " principal_name ", " x509_cert_chain ", " distinguished_name .
An asserted identity whose form is not listed is refused
.RI ( NO_PERMISSION ,
a
.B ContextError
service context attached). Empty (the default): a request may still
authenticate as itself via GSSUP; it cannot assert a different identity.
.SS naming.csiv2.gssup
.TP
.B password_file
Path to a GSSUP credential file: one
.I username:salt_hex:iterations:hash_hex
entry per line,
.IR "hash = PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA-256(password, salt, iterations)" .
No plain-text password is ever read from this file or from the
configuration. There is no built-in tool to write an entry \(em
.I zerodds_corba_csiv2::gssup_store::format_entry
is the four-field format a site script produces it with.
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/naming-svc.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-naming-svc (1).
